00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:03,220
 And so anyone will do.

530
00:22:03,220 --> 00:22:09,120
 You cannot experience intimacy without equality.

531
00:22:09,120 --> 00:22:13,480
 And here's the thing that's crazy about this.

532
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,420
 Real men are not threatened by this reality.

533
00:22:16,420 --> 00:22:20,240
 Like they actually look at the equality of women

534
00:22:20,240 --> 00:22:22,600
 and they are not threatened, they're excited about it.

535
00:22:22,600 --> 00:22:25,160
 Like you read on and you see Adam says this,

536
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,160
 he says, this is at last bone of my bones

537
00:22:28,160 --> 00:22:29,200
 and flesh of my flesh.

538
00:22:29,200 --> 00:22:33,280
 She shall be called woman because she was taken out of man.

539
00:22:33,280 --> 00:22:38,280
 Like in your Bible, that's formatted as a stanza, right?

540
00:22:38,280 --> 00:22:40,100
 Take you back to English class.

541
00:22:40,100 --> 00:22:44,400
 It doesn't look like the rest of the words on the page.

542
00:22:44,400 --> 00:22:49,400
 Like it's separated, it's indented, it's stacked multi-line.

543
00:22:49,400 --> 00:22:52,120
 And the reason why is it is trying to communicate to him,

544
00:22:52,120 --> 00:22:56,320
 communicate to us that Adam just burst into song.

545
00:22:56,320 --> 00:23:00,680
 Like that's what seeing a woman will do to a man

546
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:03,880
 that actually agrees with her God-given equality.

547
00:23:03,880 --> 00:23:06,680
 It will lead him to sing.

548
00:23:06,680 --> 00:23:08,840
 Says therefore a man shall leave his father and his mother

549
00:23:08,840 --> 00:23:10,040
 and he shall hold fast to his wife

550
00:23:10,040 --> 00:23:11,660
 and they shall become one flesh

551
00:23:11,660 --> 00:23:13,540
 and the man and his wife were both naked

552
00:23:13,540 --> 00:23:14,920
 and they were not ashamed.

553
00:23:14,920 --> 00:23:18,220
 Genesis one would summarize these ideas

554
00:23:18,220 --> 00:23:20,420
 as we went from good to very good.

555
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:22,600
 That's the way the story ends.

556
00:23:22,600 --> 00:23:26,240
 The culmination of creation as a woman comes into the scene

557
00:23:26,240 --> 00:23:28,400
 is it levels everything up

558
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:31,920
 because she is distinctly special.

559
00:23:31,920 --> 00:23:35,600
 Now with all of that said, what is the purpose of woman?

560
00:23:35,600 --> 00:23:39,480
 The first purpose is this.

561
00:23:39,480 --> 00:23:44,320
 We gotta know that women help through strength.

562
00:23:44,320 --> 00:23:48,040
 They help through strength.

563
00:23:48,040 --> 00:23:51,880
 This is what's meant by I will make a helper

564
00:23:51,880 --> 00:23:53,640
 suitable for him.

565
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:55,920
 Now, let me be very clear.

566
00:23:55,920 --> 00:23:58,440
 When it talks about a helper in this moment,

567
00:23:58,440 --> 00:24:01,120
 this is not saying that women exist to serve men

568
00:24:01,120 --> 00:24:03,080
 or cook dinner or play with babies or help at home,

569
00:24:03,080 --> 00:24:05,200
 even though those are all really amazing things.

570
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:07,800
 The Hebrew here for suitable helper

571
00:24:07,800 --> 00:24:11,640
 is two Hebrew words smashed together, etzer, connecto.

572
00:24:11,640 --> 00:24:14,440
 And those words, they don't transliterate very well

573
00:24:14,440 --> 00:24:17,740
 into English because we don't have a good parallel

574
00:24:17,740 --> 00:24:18,920
 for what they're trying to communicate.

575
00:24:18,920 --> 00:24:23,920
 They literally mean in English, she is a help against man,

576
00:24:23,920 --> 00:24:26,680
 but not in a competitive kind of way,

577
00:24:26,680 --> 00:24:28,720
 in a complimentary sort of way.

578
00:24:28,720 --> 00:24:31,840
 She is equal, but she's distinct.

579
00:24:31,840 --> 00:24:35,800
 And that actually plays to the benefit of the man.

580
00:24:35,800 --> 00:24:38,780
 She's like Shaq to Kobe.

581
00:24:38,780 --> 00:24:42,080
 How many championships did they win?

582
00:24:42,080 --> 00:24:44,520
 You know, like Kobe needed Shaq.

583
00:24:44,520 --> 00:24:47,320
 It's like Frodo and Samwise Gamgee.

584
00:24:47,320 --> 00:24:50,680
 You know, like Frodo literally was carried by that brother

585
00:24:50,680 --> 00:24:53,160
 all the way to Mount Doom.

586
00:24:53,160 --> 00:24:54,200
 If you think about it,

587
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:57,440
 we've got 22 seasons of Grey's Anatomy.

588
00:24:57,440 --> 00:25:01,240
 I don't know how much of that we should actually have

589
00:25:01,240 --> 00:25:03,080
 or how much of that should really be credited

590
00:25:03,080 --> 00:25:06,280
 to the friendship of Christina Yang and Meredith Grey.

591
00:25:06,280 --> 00:25:10,840
 I wonder if in fact we ever would have seen

592
00:25:10,840 --> 00:25:14,960
 Paulette Bonifante get her dog back, if not for Elle Woods.

593
00:25:14,960 --> 00:25:17,520
 You know, like this is what it means to have

594
00:25:17,520 --> 00:25:19,920
 a complimentary helper, someone that can step into

595
00:25:19,920 --> 00:25:22,760
 your story and uplift your purpose

596
00:25:22,760 --> 00:25:26,000
 and lead you to fulfill your responsibility.

597
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:29,520
 And this is big ladies, because I understand the word help

598
00:25:29,520 --> 00:25:33,320
 or helper or help mate can feel offensive,

599
00:25:33,320 --> 00:25:37,680
 but that word, etzer, throughout the Bible,

600
00:25:37,680 --> 00:25:41,960
 it is most often used when speaking of God himself.

601
00:25:41,960 --> 00:25:44,840
 So I'll just give you a few examples for the sake of time.

602
00:25:44,840 --> 00:25:47,120
 The first is in Deuteronomy 33 verse seven.

603
00:25:47,120 --> 00:25:48,120
 In this he said of Judah,

604
00:25:48,120 --> 00:25:52,080
 "Hear O Lord the voice of Judah and bring him to his people

605
00:25:52,080 --> 00:25:55,120
 "with your hands, contend for him and be a help."

606
00:25:55,120 --> 00:25:57,960
 There it is, against his adversaries.

607
00:25:57,960 --> 00:26:01,520
 Psalm 33 20 says, "Our soul waits for the Lord.

608
00:26:01,520 --> 00:26:05,440
 "He is our help and our shield."

609
00:26:05,440 --> 00:26:08,540
 Psalm 70 verse five says, "But I am poor and needy.

610
00:26:08,540 --> 00:26:12,160
 "Hasten to me O God, you're my help.

611
00:26:12,160 --> 00:26:14,800
 "You're my deliverer, you're my salvation."

612
00:26:14,800 --> 00:26:17,040
 Is what he's trying to say, Oh Lord, do not delay.

613
00:26:17,040 --> 00:26:19,360
 I could go on, but the point is really clear.

614
00:26:19,360 --> 00:26:21,120
 According to God, helping has less to do

615
00:26:21,120 --> 00:26:24,580
 with serving up sandwiches and more of serving up salvation.

616
00:26:24,580 --> 00:26:27,880
 That's what the scripture is trying to communicate.

617
00:26:27,880 --> 00:26:30,360
 I think this is imperative that you understand.

618
00:26:30,360 --> 00:26:34,060
 Like when we read about help in the scripture,

619
00:26:34,060 --> 00:26:37,940
 it is not communicating from a position of weakness

620
00:26:37,940 --> 00:26:39,720
 because if it is speaking of God,

621
00:26:39,720 --> 00:26:43,020
 he has never been weak once in his life.

622
00:26:43,020 --> 00:26:47,920
 Instead, the helper in any situation,

623
00:26:47,920 --> 00:26:50,680
 be it your landlord with a leaky faucet,

624
00:26:50,680 --> 00:26:53,580
 be it your mom with that stain you can't get out,

625
00:26:53,580 --> 00:26:57,840
 be it your friend processing whatever difficulty

626
00:26:57,840 --> 00:26:59,600
 you're going through, be it your doctor

627
00:26:59,600 --> 00:27:03,000
 that is stitching you up, whatever helper you have

628
00:27:03,000 --> 00:27:05,360
 in your life is functioning from a position

629
00:27:05,360 --> 00:27:09,400
 of strength and not weakness.

630
00:27:09,400 --> 00:27:14,240
 They are moving towards that which is incapable

631
00:27:14,240 --> 00:27:16,280
 and insufficient alone.

632
00:27:16,280 --> 00:27:19,760
 And it is actually strengthening it

633
00:27:19,760 --> 00:27:23,440
 to fulfill its God-given purpose.

634
00:27:23,440 --> 00:27:26,360
 So let me ask you ladies in the room a few questions.

635
00:27:26,360 --> 00:27:28,040
 Do you know your strengths?

636
00:27:28,040 --> 00:27:32,200
 Because if you don't, you will not be able

637
00:27:32,200 --> 00:27:33,960
 to make the kind of difference in life

638
00:27:33,960 --> 00:27:36,440
 that God has actually designed you to make.

639
00:27:36,440 --> 00:27:38,960
 So in my marriage, like just cards on the table,

640
00:27:38,960 --> 00:27:41,880
 my wife is far more organized than I am.

641
00:27:41,880 --> 00:27:44,520
 Like I'm an idealist, she is a realist.

642
00:27:44,520 --> 00:27:48,280
 And so what that means is I often intend very well

643
00:27:48,280 --> 00:27:53,280
 and yet she needs to help me ensure that I do very well.

644
00:27:53,280 --> 00:27:55,720
 I might say like, "Yeah, baby, I'll get that done."

645
00:27:55,720 --> 00:27:57,240
 But she knows if I don't write it down,

646
00:27:57,240 --> 00:27:59,000
 I'm not gonna get that thing done.

647
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:02,180
 And so what she has done is she has created a task list.

648
00:28:02,180 --> 00:28:04,600
 Now, listen, gentlemen, there is such a thing known

649
00:28:04,600 --> 00:28:06,380
 as a honey-do list.

650
00:28:06,380 --> 00:28:07,880
 Are you aware of what this is?

651
00:28:07,880 --> 00:28:10,200
 You will be aware of it one day.

652
00:28:10,200 --> 00:28:13,120
 The honey-do list is a list that I hate.

653
00:28:13,120 --> 00:28:17,840
 But my wife is someone I love.

654
00:28:17,840 --> 00:28:21,060
 And what she is doing by way of making this list

655
00:28:21,060 --> 00:28:25,440
 is not detailing for me everything that I have to do

656
00:28:25,440 --> 00:28:27,000
 in submission to her.

657
00:28:27,000 --> 00:28:30,940
 What she's doing is she's trying to help set me up.

658
00:28:30,940 --> 00:28:34,880
 She's saving me from abdicating my responsibility as a man

659
00:28:34,880 --> 00:28:36,920
 to both provide and protect my family.

660
00:28:36,920 --> 00:28:40,320
 She is preparing me to fulfill my role

661
00:28:40,320 --> 00:28:43,720
 by way of her strength in the face of my weakness.

662
00:28:43,720 --> 00:28:45,640
 And listen, this is just one example

663
00:28:45,640 --> 00:28:48,200
 of how it happens in my marriage.

664
00:28:48,200 --> 00:28:49,680
 There are also multiple examples

665
00:28:49,680 --> 00:28:51,960
 of how this happens outside of my marriage

666
00:28:51,960 --> 00:28:54,460
 because help, as we're talking about,

667
00:28:54,460 --> 00:28:57,080
 is not constrained to a marital union.

668
00:28:57,080 --> 00:28:59,600
 It can happen between brothers and sisters.

669
00:28:59,600 --> 00:29:03,320
 And so in my life, as is true of many of yours,

670
00:29:03,320 --> 00:29:05,960
 this sort of help is happening in ministry spaces,

671
00:29:05,960 --> 00:29:07,160
 it's happening in work spaces,

672
00:29:07,160 --> 00:29:08,480
 it's happening in neighborhoods,

673
00:29:08,480 --> 00:29:10,200
 it is happening amongst your family members,

674
00:29:10,200 --> 00:29:14,340
 it is happening in all realms of your life as well as mine.

675
00:29:14,340 --> 00:29:19,880
 Because women who know their strengths

676
00:29:19,880 --> 00:29:21,900
 can better others by way of them.

677
00:29:21,900 --> 00:29:25,600
 So let me just say, ladies, you need to know your strengths.

678
00:29:25,600 --> 00:29:27,420
 How do you know your strengths?

679
00:29:27,420 --> 00:29:30,080
 Well, like, what just works whenever you do it?

680
00:29:30,080 --> 00:29:32,080
 Like, what comes really easy to you?

681
00:29:32,080 --> 00:29:34,520
 What is the thing that you do that your friends are like,

682
00:29:34,520 --> 00:29:36,680
 "Girl, you are so good at that."

683
00:29:36,680 --> 00:29:40,800
 What is it that your boss just consistently hands over to you

684
00:29:40,800 --> 00:29:43,120
 because he knows if he gives you this task,

685
00:29:43,120 --> 00:29:47,520
 it is only going to get done and it's only going to go well.

686
00:29:47,520 --> 00:29:49,640
 These are the things that will help you to identify

687
00:29:49,640 --> 00:29:51,620
 what your strengths actually are.

688
00:29:51,620 --> 00:29:53,480
 But whatever your strength is, please listen to me,

689
00:29:53,480 --> 00:29:56,840
 we need it, we need it.

690
00:29:56,840 --> 00:30:00,320
 Just as God saved his people through his strength,

691
00:30:00,320 --> 00:30:03,640
 so too will he save us through yours.

692
00:30:04,840 --> 00:30:06,080
 The second question that I would ask you

693
00:30:06,080 --> 00:30:07,760
 is do you know your limits?

694
00:30:07,760 --> 00:30:10,100
 Do you know your limits?

695
00:30:10,100 --> 00:30:11,040
 Because I hate to break it to you,

696
00:30:11,040 --> 00:30:12,440
 you cannot help everybody.

697
00:30:12,440 --> 00:30:17,880
 Like some of you, you're trying to help your man

698
00:30:17,880 --> 00:30:19,020
 by leading him to Jesus.

699
00:30:19,020 --> 00:30:21,040
 I call you guys the avenged daters.

700
00:30:21,040 --> 00:30:25,880
 And the truth of the matter is you spend time around him.

701
00:30:25,880 --> 00:30:28,200
 You think he's cute, you got some chemistry,

702
00:30:28,200 --> 00:30:29,660
 he's gone to church with you,

703
00:30:29,660 --> 00:30:32,000
 he actually has made some memories

704
00:30:32,000 --> 00:30:33,340
 and he's cool with you being a Christian

705
00:30:33,340 --> 00:30:36,520
 even though he has no interest in it of himself.

706
00:30:36,520 --> 00:30:38,320
 But can I just level with you for a minute?

707
00:30:38,320 --> 00:30:41,440
 No different than you can lead a horse to water,

708
00:30:41,440 --> 00:30:42,400
 but you cannot make a drink.

709
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:44,680
 So too, can you take a man to church,

710
00:30:44,680 --> 00:30:47,040
 but you cannot help him believe.

711
00:30:47,040 --> 00:30:48,600
 That's on God.

712
00:30:48,600 --> 00:30:50,880
 Some men,

713
00:30:50,880 --> 00:30:58,640
 some men will not be helped

714
00:30:58,640 --> 00:31:01,720
 because they will not receive your help.

715
00:31:03,560 --> 00:31:04,820
 And so the best thing you can do

716
00:31:04,820 --> 00:31:05,960
 if you were in that situation

717
00:31:05,960 --> 00:31:08,880
 and this is going to feel cold,

718
00:31:08,880 --> 00:31:11,820
 it might feel calculated,

719
00:31:11,820 --> 00:31:16,640
 but I promise I mean it in the best way

720
00:31:16,640 --> 00:31:17,940
 'cause I think it will not only help you,

721
00:31:17,940 --> 00:31:18,980
 but it will help him.

722
00:31:18,980 --> 00:31:22,320
 You have to end that relationship

723
00:31:22,320 --> 00:31:23,760
 because as you end that relationship,

724
00:31:23,760 --> 00:31:27,200
 what will happen is he will realize

725
00:31:27,200 --> 00:31:29,840
 just how serious you are about your faith

726
00:31:29,840 --> 00:31:32,120
 and that might be the beginning of him considering

727
00:31:32,120 --> 00:31:34,080
 how serious he should be about his own.

728
00:31:34,080 --> 00:31:37,320
 Some men will not be helped

729
00:31:37,320 --> 00:31:38,840
 because they do not want to be helped,

730
00:31:38,840 --> 00:31:42,080
 but the beauty of the story is Christ Jesus

731
00:31:42,080 --> 00:31:45,640
 moved towards us when we did not want his help.

732
00:31:45,640 --> 00:31:47,200
 And yet he offered to us the help

733
00:31:47,200 --> 00:31:49,880
 we did not know we needed.

734
00:31:49,880 --> 00:31:52,280
 And so by you vacating that seat,

735
00:31:52,280 --> 00:31:53,880
 you will create space for Christ

736
00:31:53,880 --> 00:31:55,300
 to do what only he can do.

737
00:31:55,300 --> 00:31:57,640
 You let God be God, you be you.

738
00:31:57,640 --> 00:31:58,480
 That's the first.

739
00:31:58,480 --> 00:32:01,040
 The second group that I think I just need to talk to

740
00:32:03,120 --> 00:32:05,480
 is a group of you that need to know

741
00:32:05,480 --> 00:32:07,400
 some people are beyond your help.

742
00:32:07,400 --> 00:32:14,120
 Some of you, out of a desire to be gracious

743
00:32:14,120 --> 00:32:15,760
 and long-suffering,

744
00:32:15,760 --> 00:32:20,760
 you have tolerated selfish and coercive

745
00:32:20,760 --> 00:32:25,220
 and belittling behavior from boys

746
00:32:25,220 --> 00:32:30,200
 that know nothing about sacrificial love and leadership.

747
00:32:30,200 --> 00:32:32,600
 And the reason they don't know about sacrificial love

748
00:32:32,600 --> 00:32:34,920
 and leadership is they do not know the God

749
00:32:34,920 --> 00:32:38,120
 that has sacrificed himself out of his love

750
00:32:38,120 --> 00:32:40,960
 and in his leadership for his people's sake.

751
00:32:40,960 --> 00:32:44,680
 And yet you're sitting here and you're so concerned

752
00:32:44,680 --> 00:32:48,520
 that if you're not the one to stay in his life,

753
00:32:48,520 --> 00:32:50,960
 to shore up your commitment,

754
00:32:50,960 --> 00:32:52,920
 he might never come to know Jesus.

755
00:32:52,920 --> 00:32:56,420
 The truth of the matter is you are sacrificing yourself

756
00:32:56,420 --> 00:32:59,160
 when Jesus has already sacrificed himself.

757
00:32:59,160 --> 00:33:01,160
 You do not need to lay down your life

758
00:33:01,160 --> 00:33:03,040
 for the sake of that man.

759
00:33:03,040 --> 00:33:04,240
 They need to know about the man

760
00:33:04,240 --> 00:33:08,000
 that has already laid down his life for the sake of them.

761
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:09,720
 And so you just need to give space to it.

762
00:33:09,720 --> 00:33:11,160
 You need to back away from it.

763
00:33:11,160 --> 00:33:14,800
 You need to preserve the fact that he is not,

764
00:33:14,800 --> 00:33:17,920
 he is not taking the life you're wanting to receive.

765
00:33:17,920 --> 00:33:20,760
 Instead, he is robbing you of the life

766
00:33:20,760 --> 00:33:22,600
 that Christ has come to give.

767
00:33:22,600 --> 00:33:24,420
 So move out of the way and let Christ do

768
00:33:24,420 --> 00:33:25,960
 what Christ wants to do.

769
00:33:25,960 --> 00:33:30,960
 He will actually move towards those that are beyond our help

770
00:33:30,960 --> 00:33:34,440
 because no one is too far gone

771
00:33:34,440 --> 00:33:39,440
 or is too difficult to find or too hard to reach for Christ.

772
00:33:39,440 --> 00:33:41,360
 He can help anyone.

773
00:33:41,360 --> 00:33:45,880
 For we all were at one time beyond help, beyond saving.

774
00:33:45,880 --> 00:33:48,240
 And yet he stepped in and he saved the day.

775
00:33:48,240 --> 00:33:49,760
 He helped us all.

776
00:33:49,760 --> 00:33:52,620
 Last question.

777
00:33:52,620 --> 00:33:55,180
 Do you know your situation?

778
00:33:56,160 --> 00:33:57,160
 Because here's the thing,

779
00:33:57,160 --> 00:33:59,760
 your purpose as a helper to offer your strength

780
00:33:59,760 --> 00:34:01,000
 in service of someone's weakness

781
00:34:01,000 --> 00:34:02,840
 does not just begin in marriage.

782
00:34:02,840 --> 00:34:06,440
 So listen to me, ladies, what's your situation right now?

783
00:34:06,440 --> 00:34:08,680
 Whatever your situation is right now,

784
00:34:08,680 --> 00:34:11,760
 the opportunity to help through your strength is available.

785
00:34:11,760 --> 00:34:13,640
 You do not need to be married, as I've already said,

786
00:34:13,640 --> 00:34:16,040
 so you don't need to wait on a man any longer.

787
00:34:16,040 --> 00:34:18,000
 Like just, there's so many examples.

788
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:19,880
 I could give you two quick examples.

789
00:34:19,880 --> 00:34:22,680
 Like one is an example of a single friend

790
00:34:22,680 --> 00:34:24,860
 that I knew when I worked in college ministry

791
00:34:24,860 --> 00:34:26,200
 in College Station, Texas.

792
00:34:26,200 --> 00:34:28,640
 She left an advertising agency in New York.

793
00:34:28,640 --> 00:34:32,320
 She moved all the way to small town, Texas.

794
00:34:32,320 --> 00:34:35,360
 And she took over a ministry that has blessed the lives

795
00:34:35,360 --> 00:34:39,240
 of thousands of young women all across the city

796
00:34:39,240 --> 00:34:42,480
 because she knew her moment was now.

797
00:34:42,480 --> 00:34:45,880
 Another dear friend of mine, she's a single lady in Houston.

798
00:34:45,880 --> 00:34:46,920
 At least she was a single lady

799
00:34:46,920 --> 00:34:48,440
 at the time she's married today.

800
00:34:48,440 --> 00:34:50,040
 But during her singleness,

801
00:34:50,040 --> 00:34:53,120
 she realized there were so many other women,

802
00:34:53,120 --> 00:34:56,360
 young, single adults in our city, in our ministry,

803
00:34:56,360 --> 00:34:58,960
 that were trapped under all of these taboo topics

804
00:34:58,960 --> 00:35:00,720
 that they had never spoken aloud

805
00:35:00,720 --> 00:35:02,200
 until she organized an evening.

806
00:35:02,200 --> 00:35:05,840
 Like she dreamt it, she developed it, she directed it.

807
00:35:05,840 --> 00:35:08,000
 She did all of it.

808
00:35:08,000 --> 00:35:12,020
 And the fruit that was felt from the freedom that was found

809
00:35:12,020 --> 00:35:16,160
 is still being experienced today, years later.

810
00:35:16,160 --> 00:35:18,660
 These are women that knew their situation,

811
00:35:18,660 --> 00:35:20,200
 that knew their strengths,

812
00:35:20,200 --> 00:35:23,520
 and they did not wait for some man to ask 'em out

813
00:35:23,520 --> 00:35:25,320
 and take 'em to dinner and put a ring on.

814
00:35:25,320 --> 00:35:27,040
 They just went for it.

815
00:35:27,040 --> 00:35:28,360
 They were game.

816
00:35:28,360 --> 00:35:29,440
 They were ready.

817
00:35:29,440 --> 00:35:31,120
 They wanted to play ball.

818
00:35:31,120 --> 00:35:32,280
 And the truth of the matter is,

819
00:35:32,280 --> 00:35:34,520
 they have made a massive difference in the lives of people

820
00:35:34,520 --> 00:35:37,560
 for the glory of God, because they said, yes.

821
00:35:37,560 --> 00:35:39,080
 Won't you do the same?

822
00:35:39,080 --> 00:35:40,320
 Won't you do the same?

823
00:35:40,320 --> 00:35:43,880
 Numerous stories of redemption in the Bible

824
00:35:43,880 --> 00:35:46,500
 begin with women because they decided to act.

825
00:35:46,500 --> 00:35:50,400
 They decided to help Eve, Hagar, Leah, Shifra, Empua,

826
00:35:50,400 --> 00:35:52,800
 Miriam, Samson's mother, Ruth, Hannah, Esther,

827
00:35:52,800 --> 00:35:55,120
 Elizabeth, Mary, all of them helped

828
00:35:55,120 --> 00:35:58,280
 while Israel was being oppressed by foolish or evil men.

829
00:35:58,280 --> 00:36:00,400
 Women judged Israel, Deborah.

830
00:36:00,400 --> 00:36:02,480
 They won military victories, Jael.

831
00:36:02,480 --> 00:36:04,320
 Women saved their husbands, Abigail,

832
00:36:04,320 --> 00:36:06,360
 their children, Jochebed, their city,

833
00:36:06,360 --> 00:36:08,640
 the Tekoaite woman, and their nation, Esther.

834
00:36:08,640 --> 00:36:11,240
 Women prophesied, Holda and Philip's daughters.

835
00:36:11,240 --> 00:36:13,520
 They composed psalms and songs

836
00:36:13,520 --> 00:36:15,800
 that appear in the scripture, Hannah and Mary.

837
00:36:15,800 --> 00:36:18,800
 They explained the word of God to men, Priscilla.

838
00:36:18,800 --> 00:36:20,480
 They hosted churches, Chloe.

839
00:36:20,480 --> 00:36:22,080
 They ran businesses, Lydia.

840
00:36:22,080 --> 00:36:24,120
 They served as deacons and patrons, Phoebe.

841
00:36:24,120 --> 00:36:27,640
 They co-labored with Paul in the gospel, Euodia,

842
00:36:27,640 --> 00:36:31,160
 and they are identified among the apostles, Junia.

843
00:36:31,160 --> 00:36:33,960
 All of these women, they knew their situation.

844
00:36:33,960 --> 00:36:35,160
 They knew how they could help.

845
00:36:35,160 --> 00:36:40,160
 And they said, yes, do you know your situation,

846
00:36:40,160 --> 00:36:42,280
 how you can help?

847
00:36:42,280 --> 00:36:44,520
 And are you willing to say yes?

848
00:36:44,520 --> 00:36:47,040
 Women have been making a difference for a very long time

849
00:36:47,040 --> 00:36:49,260
 in the capacity of suitable helper.

850
00:36:49,260 --> 00:36:51,900
 The question is, will you?

851
00:36:51,900 --> 00:36:57,480
 Let me say one more thing before I move on.

852
00:36:57,480 --> 00:37:02,800
 And the only reason why I'm saying

853
00:37:02,800 --> 00:37:04,360
 is 'cause it's come up in conversation a couple of times.

854
00:37:04,360 --> 00:37:05,880
 It came up in Q and A a couple of weeks ago,

855
00:37:05,880 --> 00:37:08,800
 and I just wanna make sure it's abundantly clear.

856
00:37:08,800 --> 00:37:11,520
 Sisters, you do not need to shrink yourself

857
00:37:12,380 --> 00:37:15,720
 for fear of intimidating some man by way of your strength,

858
00:37:15,720 --> 00:37:17,320
 your boldness, or your maturity.

859
00:37:17,320 --> 00:37:20,040
 We don't need you to sit down.

860
00:37:20,040 --> 00:37:21,680
 The church needs men to stand up.

861
00:37:21,680 --> 00:37:26,760
 So please, do not shrink yourself

862
00:37:26,760 --> 00:37:30,760
 in the place where men need to grow.

863
00:37:30,760 --> 00:37:34,240
 And gentlemen, I'm not trying to low blow

864
00:37:34,240 --> 00:37:37,000
 or throw unnecessary jabs.

865
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:42,000
 If this is frustrating or convicting or rude,

866
00:37:42,400 --> 00:37:45,200
 resonating, the spirit might be speaking

867
00:37:45,200 --> 00:37:48,040
 to a room full of women by way of a message on women,

868
00:37:48,040 --> 00:37:51,480
 but he might actually be trying to talk to you.

869
00:37:51,480 --> 00:37:55,880
 He might be inviting you into more of his purpose as well.

870
00:37:55,880 --> 00:38:02,640
 Second purpose of woman.

871
00:38:02,640 --> 00:38:03,680
 We see it in the next chapter.

872
00:38:03,680 --> 00:38:05,520
 Flip over to chapter three.

873
00:38:05,520 --> 00:38:07,600
 What we see in chapter three

874
00:38:07,600 --> 00:38:10,240
 is right after mankind's rebellion,

875
00:38:10,240 --> 00:38:13,060
 they sin against God, they eat of the forbidden fruit.

876
00:38:13,060 --> 00:38:17,080
 We see God, he tells them the consequences of their actions

877
00:38:17,080 --> 00:38:20,080
 and in their following, we read this.

878
00:38:20,080 --> 00:38:22,960
 In verse 20, the man called his wife's name Eve

879
00:38:22,960 --> 00:38:24,680
 because she was the mother of all living.

880
00:38:24,680 --> 00:38:26,860
 And the Lord God made for Adam and for his wife,

881
00:38:26,860 --> 00:38:28,160
 garments of skin, and he clothed them.

882
00:38:28,160 --> 00:38:29,840
 Now, this is a really interesting moment

883
00:38:29,840 --> 00:38:30,800
 in the story of Adam and Eve

884
00:38:30,800 --> 00:38:34,240
 because this is right after they royally messed up

885
00:38:34,240 --> 00:38:35,640
 and yet it is right before

886
00:38:35,640 --> 00:38:36,760
 they have been kicked out of the garden,

887
00:38:36,760 --> 00:38:39,080
 meaning they have broken everything

888
00:38:39,080 --> 00:38:42,680
 and yet they have not been sent out into that brokenness.

889
00:38:42,680 --> 00:38:46,560
 And what's crazy about this moment is in the middle of it,

890
00:38:46,560 --> 00:38:49,640
 we see, while still in the garden, in the presence of God,

891
00:38:49,640 --> 00:38:51,760
 we learn the second purpose of woman,

892
00:38:51,760 --> 00:38:55,640
 which is this, to nurture and empower others.

893
00:38:55,640 --> 00:38:59,140
 See, for the first time, Eve is actually named.

894
00:38:59,140 --> 00:39:00,720
 We've known that her name is Eve

895
00:39:00,720 --> 00:39:02,680
 just because we've grown up in Christian circles

896
00:39:02,680 --> 00:39:04,800
 and yet this is the moment when she gets her name

897
00:39:04,800 --> 00:39:07,080
 and her name means mother of all living.

898
00:39:07,080 --> 00:39:10,180
 Yeah, what's interesting is she's not even a mom at this time

899
00:39:10,180 --> 00:39:12,040
 like there are no kids in the picture.

900
00:39:12,040 --> 00:39:13,620
 She is a mom.

901
00:39:13,620 --> 00:39:16,580
 She is not yet a mother in reality

902
00:39:16,580 --> 00:39:18,620
 and yet Adam chooses to give her this name.

903
00:39:18,620 --> 00:39:19,720
 Anyways, why is that?

904
00:39:19,720 --> 00:39:20,560
 It's a couple of reasons.

905
00:39:20,560 --> 00:39:22,980
 Number one, she is a mother,

906
00:39:22,980 --> 00:39:26,400
 biologically capable of being a mom by design.

907
00:39:26,400 --> 00:39:28,520
 And then two, she will be a mother

908
00:39:28,520 --> 00:39:30,960
 according to God's promise.

909
00:39:30,960 --> 00:39:33,480
 So by design, the female body produces

910
00:39:33,480 --> 00:39:35,280
 a large amount of oxytocin,

911
00:39:35,280 --> 00:39:36,960
 promoting bonding and affiliation.

912
00:39:36,960 --> 00:39:40,040
 And that ultimately enhances a woman's maternal instinct

913
00:39:40,040 --> 00:39:44,000
 in a way that exceeds regular men.

914
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:46,840
 If you want to see this play out in reality,

915
00:39:46,840 --> 00:39:48,940
 look at new moms and new dads.

916
00:39:48,940 --> 00:39:51,280
 New moms receive their newborn.

917
00:39:51,280 --> 00:39:52,560
 It's like they've been doing it their whole life.

918
00:39:52,560 --> 00:39:54,120
 They just spring into action.

919
00:39:54,120 --> 00:39:56,740
 They know already instinctively how to change diapers

920
00:39:56,740 --> 00:39:59,760
 and they're prepared to wake up at all hours of the night

921
00:39:59,760 --> 00:40:02,480
 and yet you hand a newborn to a man

922
00:40:02,480 --> 00:40:05,400
 and some of you guys are nervously laughing

923
00:40:05,400 --> 00:40:07,080
 'cause you know you're like, "Am I gonna drop this thing,

924
00:40:07,080 --> 00:40:09,800
 "man, I've never been more uncomfortable in my life."

925
00:40:09,800 --> 00:40:12,000
 It's because women have a more natural,

926
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:14,900
 biological maternal instinct.

927
00:40:14,900 --> 00:40:19,060
 There's a natural instinct that is God given.

928
00:40:19,060 --> 00:40:22,060
 I love the way Elizabeth Elliot wrote to her own daughter

929
00:40:22,060 --> 00:40:24,240
 about the meaning of womanhood.

930
00:40:24,240 --> 00:40:28,280
 She said this, she said, "Yours is the body of a woman.

931
00:40:28,280 --> 00:40:29,660
 "What does it signify to you?

932
00:40:29,660 --> 00:40:32,140
 "Is there invisible meaning in its invisible signs,

933
00:40:32,140 --> 00:40:33,560
 "the softness, the smoothness,

934
00:40:33,560 --> 00:40:35,620
 "the lighter bone and muscle structure, the breasts,

935
00:40:35,620 --> 00:40:36,800
 "the womb?

936
00:40:36,800 --> 00:40:40,240
 "Are they utterly unrelated to what you yourself are?

937
00:40:40,240 --> 00:40:43,040
 "Isn't your identity intimately bound up

938
00:40:43,040 --> 00:40:45,680
 "with these material forms?"

939
00:40:45,680 --> 00:40:49,620
 See, women are biologically designed to nurture

940
00:40:49,620 --> 00:40:51,720
 in that your bodies are crafted by God

941
00:40:51,720 --> 00:40:55,760
 to incubate and sustain a child's life.

942
00:40:55,760 --> 00:40:57,960
 But it's not just that.

943
00:40:57,960 --> 00:40:59,800
 It's actually so much more.

944
00:40:59,800 --> 00:41:02,760
 You're not just biologically designed to be a mother,

945
00:41:02,760 --> 00:41:06,720
 you are spiritually destined to be a mother.

946
00:41:06,720 --> 00:41:08,840
 Which is why the role of motherhood

947
00:41:08,840 --> 00:41:12,800
 is not for women that have children alone.

948
00:41:12,800 --> 00:41:16,820
 It is available to all women, regardless of your station.

949
00:41:16,820 --> 00:41:19,480
 Because though children were the prize of a family

950
00:41:19,480 --> 00:41:20,320
 in the Old Testament,

951
00:41:20,320 --> 00:41:23,400
 the prize of a family in the New are disciples.

952
00:41:23,400 --> 00:41:25,600
 And we see this, it's fascinating.

953
00:41:25,600 --> 00:41:29,240
 As God promises to Eve that she will have a son,

954
00:41:29,240 --> 00:41:31,040
 she has no children yet.

955
00:41:31,040 --> 00:41:35,120
 That child is not just one that will be biologically

956
00:41:35,120 --> 00:41:40,040
 from her womb, but will be spiritually for the world.

957
00:41:40,040 --> 00:41:41,760
 Because he will be the son that will crush the head

958
00:41:41,760 --> 00:41:44,360
 of the serpent, and as a result of that son,

959
00:41:44,360 --> 00:41:47,520
 life will be given, where death was in fact found.

960
00:41:47,520 --> 00:41:49,640
 So, what does this mean?

961
00:41:49,640 --> 00:41:52,000
 Does this mean that you're destined

962
00:41:52,000 --> 00:41:53,240
 to be a stay-at-home mom?

963
00:41:53,240 --> 00:41:57,040
 Like, you're getting the news right now.

964
00:41:57,040 --> 00:42:00,140
 You ain't got any kids, but guess what, girl?

965
00:42:00,140 --> 00:42:01,400
 You're gonna be a sourdough batty.

966
00:42:01,400 --> 00:42:03,320
 You know, like, you're gonna make the home

967
00:42:03,320 --> 00:42:05,560
 and cook the meals, and you're gonna take care of the kids.

968
00:42:05,560 --> 00:42:07,720
 For some of you, that sounds like your worst nightmare.

969
00:42:07,720 --> 00:42:09,520
 For others of you, you're here, and your fingers are crossed,

970
00:42:09,520 --> 00:42:10,800
 and your toes are crossed, 'cause you're praying

971
00:42:10,800 --> 00:42:12,400
 that that would actually be true.

972
00:42:12,400 --> 00:42:13,760
 That's not what I'm saying.

973
00:42:13,760 --> 00:42:20,600
 Your ability to nurture others is not limited

974
00:42:20,600 --> 00:42:21,840
 to being a biological mother.

975
00:42:21,840 --> 00:42:24,360
 It transcends it by becoming a spiritual mother.

976
00:42:24,360 --> 00:42:26,680
 Paul writes to Titus, and he says this in Titus 2.

977
00:42:26,680 --> 00:42:28,560
 He says, "Likewise, teach the older women

978
00:42:28,560 --> 00:42:30,120
 "to be reverent in the way they live,

979
00:42:30,120 --> 00:42:32,280
 "not to be slanderers or addicted to much wine,

980
00:42:32,280 --> 00:42:33,800
 "but to teach what is good.

981
00:42:33,800 --> 00:42:35,560
 "Then they can urge the younger women,

982
00:42:35,560 --> 00:42:37,280
 "not necessarily their daughters,

983
00:42:37,280 --> 00:42:39,780
 "but they can urge younger women, teach younger women

984
00:42:39,780 --> 00:42:41,360
 "to love their husbands and their children."

985
00:42:41,360 --> 00:42:43,080
 Do you hear what this is saying?

986
00:42:43,080 --> 00:42:46,480
 Like, you don't have to be a stay-at-home mom

987
00:42:46,480 --> 00:42:48,240
 with a harem full of kids

988
00:42:48,240 --> 00:42:50,600
 and the next television spot on TLC,

989
00:42:50,600 --> 00:42:53,680
 nor do you have to be some sort of girl boss influencer

990
00:42:53,680 --> 00:42:55,680
 that's running a Fortune 500

991
00:42:55,680 --> 00:42:58,940
 to know your purpose is to nurture other people.

992
00:42:58,940 --> 00:43:02,760
 It is the purpose of your life, ladies, across the board.

993
00:43:02,760 --> 00:43:05,980
 Now, I have notes here to talk to each of you individually,

994
00:43:05,980 --> 00:43:07,880
 those of you that wanna be stay-at-home moms,

995
00:43:07,880 --> 00:43:10,880
 and those of you that wanna actually be a working woman

996
00:43:10,880 --> 00:43:11,700
 for the rest of your life.

997
00:43:11,700 --> 00:43:14,760
 For the sake of time, I am not going to get into it.

998
00:43:14,760 --> 00:43:17,040
 Here's the simple and short of it.

999
00:43:17,040 --> 00:43:18,200
 If you wanna be a stay-at-home mom,

1000
00:43:18,200 --> 00:43:20,000
 we do not need more housewives in DFW.

1001
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:21,900
 We need more disciplers in DFW.

1002
00:43:23,920 --> 00:43:25,760
 And then if you wanna be a working woman,

1003
00:43:25,760 --> 00:43:28,640
 I implore you to know, you do not need to be a girl boss

1004
00:43:28,640 --> 00:43:30,600
 when you are already a daughter of the king.

1005
00:43:30,600 --> 00:43:33,360
 You go and you use all of your giftedness,

1006
00:43:33,360 --> 00:43:35,960
 all of your skill, all of your intelligence,

1007
00:43:35,960 --> 00:43:38,840
 all of your fearlessness to the glory of God.

1008
00:43:38,840 --> 00:43:42,240
 You work so long as it is expanding his kingdom.

1009
00:43:42,240 --> 00:43:44,440
 You go, girl.

1010
00:43:44,440 --> 00:43:47,560
 (congregation laughing)

1011
00:43:47,560 --> 00:43:50,080
 God has innately given women a stronger orientation

1012
00:43:50,080 --> 00:43:51,360
 towards relationships than men.

1013
00:43:51,360 --> 00:43:55,120
 It's the reason why ladies never go to the bathroom alone.

1014
00:43:55,120 --> 00:43:56,680
 That's why you grew up going to sleepovers

1015
00:43:56,680 --> 00:43:57,520
 and fellows never did.

1016
00:43:57,520 --> 00:43:59,420
 It's why you get your nails done together.

1017
00:43:59,420 --> 00:44:02,480
 It's why immediately following that date with that guy,

1018
00:44:02,480 --> 00:44:03,800
 you're texting your friends

1019
00:44:03,800 --> 00:44:04,720
 and letting them know how things go,

1020
00:44:04,720 --> 00:44:06,920
 if not while still at the date with that guy,

1021
00:44:06,920 --> 00:44:08,980
 texting your friends and letting them know how it's going,

1022
00:44:08,980 --> 00:44:12,100
 because you are nurturers by nature.

1023
00:44:12,100 --> 00:44:18,000
 Now, nurture us.

1024
00:44:18,000 --> 00:44:18,880
 We need you to.

1025
00:44:18,880 --> 00:44:21,020
 The way that Christ has nurtured us,

1026
00:44:21,020 --> 00:44:22,800
 so to follow in his example,

1027
00:44:22,800 --> 00:44:25,440
 the very way that he looked upon the death,

1028
00:44:25,440 --> 00:44:28,480
 the sting of death across the world,

1029
00:44:28,480 --> 00:44:33,480
 and he moved towards it with life-giving sacrifice.

1030
00:44:33,480 --> 00:44:35,320
 Won't you do the same thing?

1031
00:44:35,320 --> 00:44:40,320
 See, is the sting of death true in your neighborhood,

1032
00:44:40,320 --> 00:44:41,560
 true among your roommates,

1033
00:44:41,560 --> 00:44:44,160
 true in the mundanity of your workplace?

1034
00:44:44,160 --> 00:44:45,560
 Is it true amongst your family?

1035
00:44:45,560 --> 00:44:47,720
 Where do you sense the sting of death

1036
00:44:47,720 --> 00:44:49,800
 and move into those spaces to nurture

1037
00:44:49,800 --> 00:44:52,140
 for the good of other people and the glory of God,

1038
00:44:52,140 --> 00:44:54,780
 because that is your design?

1039
00:44:54,780 --> 00:44:55,720
 And then last one.

1040
00:44:55,720 --> 00:45:00,800
 And we're gonna move out of the creation account.

1041
00:45:00,800 --> 00:45:02,640
 We're gonna roll over to 1 Peter 3.

1042
00:45:02,640 --> 00:45:04,060
 So if you have a Bible, you can turn there with me.

1043
00:45:04,060 --> 00:45:05,620
 While we're doing this, let me just say,

1044
00:45:05,620 --> 00:45:07,440
 this passage is a passage to wives.

1045
00:45:07,440 --> 00:45:09,660
 I committed to you that I'm not gonna teach about roles.

1046
00:45:09,660 --> 00:45:11,160
 I'm not teaching about roles,

1047
00:45:11,160 --> 00:45:14,200
 but I do think this passage is explicitly teaching

1048
00:45:14,200 --> 00:45:17,280
 the third and final purpose of woman that you need to know.

1049
00:45:17,280 --> 00:45:19,380
 And so I want you to see it from the text.

1050
00:45:19,380 --> 00:45:22,920
 This is what it says, 1 Peter 3, one through four.

1051
00:45:22,920 --> 00:45:23,760
 Peter says this.

1052
00:45:23,760 --> 00:45:24,940
 He says, "Hey, wives, in the same way,

1053
00:45:24,940 --> 00:45:27,560
 "submit yourselves to your own husbands,

1054
00:45:27,560 --> 00:45:29,820
